==Enemy==
The Gardeneel Bros. are extremely weak both offensively and defensively, but they more than make up for it with a long-ranged attack that warps Cats forward by 1375 range. While this ability does teleport your cats straight into their blind spot, it can also cripple your backline attackers and allow the enemies' front lines to advance with ease, making them a force to be reckoned with in many of their appearances, most notably [[Iwa Rock Reef]] and [[Glass Slippers]].

In some other stages, such as [[Sirius (Cats of the Cosmos)/Outbreak|the Sirius Zombie Outbreak]] and [[Stars in the Tumbler]], they are utilized as a gimmick, where players need to abuse their weak Warping attack in order to teleport an attacker far beyond groups of strong enemies, bypassing these threats entirely to destroy the base with little to no resistance.

==Strategy==
If there are not many enemy attackers, then you can try to snipe the Gardeneel Bros. with a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance unit]]. There is not much trouble with them warping a stronger unit, but  snipers can end up in awkward positions with enemies inside their blindspots.

Another strategy is to use damaging meatshields like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] and [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] or spammable attackers, as they could be warped into the Gardeneel Bros's blindspot and kill them off. Likewise, sniping them with [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] is also an option, as its [[Wave Attack]] can gravely cripple if not outright eliminate them.

As mentioned before, Gardeneel Bros. can also be abused when it comes to strong melee units with low range. As they attack fairly frequently but inflict little damage, they will almost certainly teleport the likes of [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] right next to the enemy base.

